  "question": {
    "text": "An EM wave propagating in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-direction has a wavelength of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. The electric field vibrating <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-direction has maximum magnitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><msup><mi>Vm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Choose the correct equations for electric and magnetic fields if the EM wave is propagating in vacuum :",
    "image": null
  },
